<title>MEXICO: Bad weather forces closure of 23 Mexican ports.</title>
<headline>Bad weather forces closure of 23 Mexican ports.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A cold front forced the closure on Monday of 23 Mexican ports on the Gulf of Mexico coast, the Ministry of Communications and Transport said.</p>
<p>Winds of up to 75 kph and waves three metres high prompted officials to close ports in the states of Veracruz, Tabasco and Campeche, the ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>Earlier, officials at state oil company Petroleos Mexicanos said two of Mexico's three main crude shipping ports, Pajaritos and Dos Bocas, were closed due to the cold front.</p>
<p>--David Luhnow, Mexico City newsroom, +525 728-9565</p>
